ARCHITECTURE REQUIREMENTS
- Use adapter pattern for data providers
- Use service layer between API and persistence
- Use repository pattern where appropriate
- Separate ingestion, analysis, ranking, and presentation concerns
- Keep business logic out of route handlers
- Document all major modules

QUALITY REQUIREMENTS
- Strong typing and validation
- Unit tests for core services
- Integration tests for provider adapters
- Seed scripts and demo data
- Dockerized local development
- Example .env files
- README with setup instructions
- Architecture diagram in markdown
- Task checklist for future expansion

NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
- Graceful handling of provider failures
- Caching to respect free-tier limits
- Basic observability: logs, health endpoints, provider status
- Secure secret handling
- Timezone-safe timestamps
- Clear disclaimers that outputs are informational and not financial advice

IMPORTANT PRODUCT RULES
- Do not market this as guaranteed prediction.
- Do not fake confidence.
- Always show uncertainty and conflicting signals.
- Design for explainability first.
- Make it useful even if the LLM layer is disabled.
- Prefer deterministic/rules-based core analytics, with LLM used only for summarization and explanation.

